-- title:
--   Tensor additivity of extended-real quantum relative entropy
-- statement:
--   Let $\rho,\sigma$ be density operators on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space $A$ and let $\tau,\omega$ be density operators on another such space $B$. Then
--
--   $$D(\rho\otimes\tau\Vert\sigma\otimes\omega)=D(\rho\Vert\sigma)+D(\tau\Vert\omega).$$
--
--   The entropies are measured in bits and equality is in the extended real line. Support mismatches giving infinity are included. This supplies the relative-entropy block superadditivity used by regularization.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/JWang226/Continuity-of-regularized-channel-renyi-divergence/blob/e29274a69978bb499f00497481c6008befb0b84d/QuantumChannelContinuity/TensorRelative.lean#L24-L46

